 # Volume Rendering Property Configuration
 
-Also called: VTK Actor Property Configuration, Volume Rendering Pipeline Setup
+Also called: Synchronize with Volumes module, Transfer Function Setup, VTK Actor Property Configuration, VTK Volume Property Transfer Functions, Volume Property Configuration, Volume Rendering Pipeline Setup, Volume Rendering Property Configuration > Synchronize with Volumes, vtkVolumeProperty Setup
 
 ## Overview
-Configures the visual and shading properties of a volume rendering actor within a graphics pipeline. It establishes the mapping from scalar data to color and opacity, defines interpolation behavior, and sets lighting coefficients for gradient-based shading. It differs from [MAP](13234-map-volume-rendering.md) by focusing on the configuration of the rendering actor's internal state rather than the data interpolation strategy for irregular grids.
+Configures the visual and shading properties of a volume rendering actor within a graphics pipeline [S4, unofficial]. It establishes the mapping from scalar data to color and opacity, defines interpolation behavior, and sets lighting coefficients for gradient-based shading [S2, S4, unofficial]. It differs from [MAP](13234-map-volume-rendering.md) by focusing on the configuration of the rendering actor's internal state rather than the data interpolation strategy for irregular grids [G].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-- A volume rendering actor instance (e.g., `vtkVolume`).
-- A color transfer function object (e.g., `vtkLookupTable`).
-- A scalar opacity transfer function object (e.g., `vtkPiecewiseFunction`).
-- Lighting coefficients and gradient opacity thresholds.
